Package: devjam-science-titta-demo
Version: 1.4-1
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, python3-numpy, python3-pandas, python3-pil, python3-matplotlib, python3-h5py, python3-tables, python3-opencv, python3-i2mc
Recommends: xdg-user-dirs, curl, libnotify-bin
Suggests: python3-titta
Maintainer: Bob Rosbag <debian@bobrosbag.nl>
Description: Titta demo experiments and analyses for eye-tracking studies
 The demo_experiments and demo_analyses folders of Titta (Tobii
 eye-tracker toolbox), from the staging branch of github.com/dev-jam/Titta.
 .
 demo_experiments holds the PsychoPy demo experiments (read_me.py and
 others, also with Tobii Pro Lab and LSL). demo_analyses processes their
 data: trial extraction, data quality, fixation detection with I2MC,
 mapping fixations to AOIs with cumulative plots, scanpaths, heatmaps and
 gaze videos, plus run_analysis.py to run all steps in one go.
 .
 Both are installed read-only in /usr/share/titta-demo. To use them, copy
 a folder to a place of your own, for example from the link that
 setup-user-links (devjam-science-tools) puts in Desktop/tools, or with
 the menu entry "Titta demo", which copies everything to the Desktop
 (folder titta_demo). Its action "Download latest version from GitHub"
 fetches the current staging branch instead. Existing folders are never
 overwritten. The exact commit is in the file VERSION.
